text='''SAME-ARCHITECTURE TREE UNSEEN GENERALIZATION — APPROVED PROTOCOL 1.0

AUTHORIZED SCOPE
Run the full decision-tree unseen evaluation followed by the retained random-forest pilot. Do not launch the full forest study. Preserve the requested destination spelling: tree-samarchitecture.

DECISION TREES
Reuse all 25,200 four-method trade-off outcome rows byte-for-byte, all 300 original people, the 60 saved split/model banks and all seven budgets per dataset. No old action is re-solved. Nested 6/12/24 depth-four decision trees (minimum leaf 5, sqrt features). All source predictions and action feasibility are independently checked again. The saved SingleTreeReference is best reachable probability, with cost tie-break and an already-accepted factual shortcut; it is not a minimum-cost threshold solve.

RANDOM-FOREST PILOT
Six datasets; seeds 401 and 406; first saved person per seed; 6 and 24 whole forests; low/high positive budgets plus zero. Each forest has exactly 10 depth-four trees, minimum leaf 5, sqrt features, bootstrap=True and probability averaging. One whole forest is one competing model. Positive budgets: [0.5,5] for Synthetic/COMPAS/Polish/German, [2,50] for GMC, [1,10] for ACSIncome. Exactly 48 positive cells / 192 method rows plus 24 zero controls / 96 method rows: 288 total. ORPM has 100 rounds, eta=sqrt(log(m)/200), one-second one-thread calls, squared loss and best-observed worst-loss return rule. Each positive cell also has a 30-second UniformForest and 30-second DirectMinimax solve. SingleForestReference is a 30-second minimum-cost threshold solve shared across model counts (24 positive reference tasks, with analytic factual skips). No baseline receives ORPM starts or replacements. Pilot model banks/panels/results can be retained in a separately authorized full study.

BANKS AND UNSEEN PANELS
RF optimization-bank admission freezes best-of-first-96 validation accuracy minus 0.05, then selects the first 24 structurally distinct qualifying forests; predetermined maximum 1,536 candidates. Existing DT cutoffs remain unchanged. Two distinct experiments: fresh fit seeds on the same training sample (refit) and fresh outer training-row bootstrap plus fit seeds (bootstrap). RF always also retains its ordinary within-forest bootstrap. Each panel has the first 50 qualifying distinct models from a disjoint deterministic seed stream, excluding the competing-model fingerprints. Panels may share structural models with each other; they do not share optimization models. Admission uses the fixed family-specific lower validation cutoff with no upper cutoff. Maximum 4,096 candidates per panel; shortage stops that arm without silently changing the cutoff or architecture. All fitted candidate arrays, admission decisions and bootstrap indices are retained. No person/action/test-performance filtering. Freeze all banks, panels and cohorts within an arm before scoring or new recourse. Decision-tree arm: 6,000 unseen trees; forest pilot: 1,200 unseen forests plus 288 selected competing forests. No full forest optimization or seeds outside the pilot are authorized.

COHORTS AND METRICS
Original held-out people remain fixed. Report factual acceptance, acceptance gains and a separately tabulated common-recourse-needed subset (at least half reject for every nested m in 6/12/24); forest pilot does not silently reselect people. Report seen joint validity, unseen mean acceptance, all-50 joint validity, seen-to-unseen joint drop, and fixed-order all-5/10/25/50 prefixes. The original 24-tree expanded panel is not the new unseen panel. Same unseen panels score all methods/budgets/counts. Conditional seen-valid and recourse-needed subsets include supporting people and seeds. No averaging efficacy across budgets, counts or datasets. People average within seed; equal seed weights; pointwise 95% Student-t intervals (df=9 DT; df=1 pilot). Two-seed pilot inference is exploratory and underpowered. Solver numerical uncertainty is separate. Results are conditional on these splits, architectures, quality admission and refitting distributions; no arbitrary-network or population generalization claims.

INTEGRITY AND TIMING
Source hashes, copied row bytes, cohorts, trees, native sklearn probabilities, immutable/L2 constraints, forest aggregation, ORPM updates/return rule, native baseline separation and every rejection audit are verified independently. Timeouts/no incumbent are unresolved, not infeasibility. Loss fallbacks can use factual; a failed minimum-cost reference cannot claim factual as an accepted witness. No tolerance relaxation, extra optimize retry or efficacy-based gate. Completion requires reports, figures and CI tables/archive, passed verification and supervisor-confirmed exit. DT: 48 PNG/PDF figures; RF: 36 PNG/PDF figures. Separate one-thread arms run sequentially to avoid contaminating pilot timings. Caffeinate prevents idle sleep during active workers; OS suspension can delay progress. No hard deadline was adopted. Initial planning: 0.5–2 hours for DT, then 1–4 hours for the pilot, excluding implementation time. These are provisional, not guarantees. Full-forest projection uses measured whole-method wall times and shared-reference timings once, estimates 6/12/24 models and three positive budgets, flags unmeasured m12/medium-budget interpolation and reports a broad planning range. The full forest study remains stopped pending user authorization.
'''
